   PDF metadata: created 2018-08-17T10:58:21-07, modified 2020-08-06T18:13:05-07; a retailer's copy (v2/vendor/sources.txt; the maker's download page did not
   render to this host). Revision identifier printed on the sheet: NONE (no 'Rev', 'Revision' or 'Version' mark on either page)
   p.2: Pmax 100 W, Vmp 18.9 V, Imp 5.29 A, Voc 22.5 V, Isc 5.75 A; 36 cells (4 x 9); maximum system voltage 600 V DC;
     maximum series fuse rating 15 A; 1219 x 549 x 2 mm, 1.9 kg; Pmax -0.42 %/K, Voc -0.31 %/K, Isc +0.05 %/K; NOCT 45 +-2 C;
     operating -40 to +85 C; connectors 30 A, 1000 V DC; output cables 12 AWG
   THE REVISION IS NOT SETTLED BY THE HELD SHEET: it carries no revision mark. The owner's review reports Renogy's current US
   page for the family: Voc 24.4 V, maximum series fuse 15 A, 1093 x 582 mm (not held; compared, not substituted).
   If the kit's panels were that revision, 2S2P's open circuit would read 55.61 V at -20 C cells, 58.63 V at -40 C and 61.00 V
   by the 1.25 clause (INFERRED with the HELD sheet's -0.31 %/K: the current page's coefficient is not read here): OVER the
   coordinator's 60 V safety extra-low-voltage ceiling (array_calc.out 2: 'the standard behind it is not held'), where the
   held sheet gives 56.25 V. Its Vmp, Imp and Isc are not in the review; the stage's fixed input point
   (R8, R9: 34.29 V, a1solar ARRAY.md 3) and its 0.990 ratio are derived from the held sheet's Vmp and would move with them

2. AVAILABLE ARRAY POWER (2S2P, 4 panels)
   at STC: 400 W (MAKER, 4 x 100 W, no tolerance published)
   at 1000 W/m2 and +70 C cells: 329.9 W (MODELED, array_calc.out 5, the single-diode fit)
   at 1000 W/m2 and -20 C cells: 475.6 W (INFERRED, the sheet's Pmax coefficient applied linearly over 45 K); with the
     edge-of-cloud factor 1.25 on the irradiance, a bound of 594.5 W for a transient (INFERRED)
   on SC-37's mean day at 40/0, the largest hour into the stage: 194.3 W (TYP) and 178.6 W (WAB) (MODELED, hf_wab.out 4)

3. THE CONVERTER'S INPUT POWER: NOT A CONTROLLED LIMIT AS DRAWN
   the 200 W is the energy model's window on the stage's input (energy_two_pack.py node_power: min(panel, window))
   NETLIST: U5 LT8705A pins 30, 31 (CSNOUT, CSPOUT) on TRK_OUT and 32, 33 (CSNIN, CSPIN) on PV_P, with no resistor between: the input and output current regulation is NOT used
     (MAKER, 8705af pp.11 and 12: CSNOUT 'Connect this pin to VOUT when not in use', p.11; CSPIN 'Connect this pin to VIN
     when not in use', p.12). So the stage takes what its load asks, up to its own
     inductor current limit, from what the array gives
   what the load asks (r11dep, the front end's input is the stage's output): 144.1 W out in service, 154.9 W into the stage at
     0.93 DECLARED; 210.5 W out at the front end's highest permitted current (226.3 W in)
   the stage's own ceiling: its buck valley limit at the maximum, 20.4 A at TRK_OUT's 15.1 V: 308.0 W out, 331.2 W in (INFERRED:
     the valley threshold taken as the average it passes; the maker notes it rises at higher duty, 8705af p.22)
   the stage's input is therefore min(the array's available power, the load's demand over the efficiency, its own ceiling):
   up to 226.3 W with a load at the front end's maximum, against the model's 200 W (INFERRED)

4. COLD OPEN-CIRCUIT EXPOSURE (the string is two panels in series; the strings in parallel add no voltage)
   Voc 22.5 V a panel: 51.28 V at -20 C cells (the envelope's in-use minimum), 54.07 V at -40 C (the panel's own limit),
     56.25 V by the 1.25 clause on STC (SunPower 524958 Rev F 3.0, held back): the voltage basis 56.25 V (INFERRED)
   against: the panel's 600 V system voltage; the LT8705A's 80 V (8705af pp.2, 3); the coordinator's 60 V ceiling (its standard
     not held); board E's PV_P parts as
     generated (60 V FETs, 35 V and 50 V capacitors, a 28 V TVS, gen_sch_e.py; a1solar ARRAY.md 6, gated on REQ-016)

5. SHORT-CIRCUIT AND FAULT CURRENTS (hot cells +70 C at 1000 W/m2; the edge-of-cloud factor 1.25)
   a string: Isc 5.75 A at STC, 5.88 A hot, 7.35 A with the factor; the array: 11.50 A, 11.76 A, 14.70 A
   (a) a short at the array's output, in the lead or at the entry: the array is a current source and delivers at most
       14.70 A; F2 never opens on it; every conductor from the array to the stage carries it continuously (INFERRED)
   (b) a fault inside one string: the other string back-feeds it with at most 7.35 A (INFERRED)
   (c) a back-feed from the kit into the array (NETLIST topology): VIN_RAW -> Q2 (VIN_RAW to TRK_OUT, the ideal diode U4 LM74700-Q1,
       blocking) -> TRK_OUT -> Q6 M4 (TRK_OUT to TRK_SW2) -> L1 -> Q3 M1's body diode (TRK_SW1 to PV_P) -> PV_P -> F2 -> the array. It
       needs Q2 or U4 failed (a single fault) while M4 conducts with VIN_RAW above the panel, and its sustained source is the
       vehicle entry, limited by its LM5069 at 6.15 A unless that entry has failed too (INFERRED; the fault tree is owed)

6. STRING VERSUS COMBINED-FEED PROTECTION
   the maker's maximum series fuse rating 15 A (p.2), read as the current a module may carry in reverse (INFERRED: the usual
     meaning; the applicable standard is not held)
   (b)'s 7.35 A is under 15 A: NO STRING FUSE is needed for faults inside the array (INFERRED; a1solar ARRAY.md 1 and 4)
   F2 sits in the COMBINED feed (NETLIST: F2 between PV_IN and PV_P). At 20 A it exceeds one string's 15 A, so F2 does not protect a
     single string: with one string disconnected, a back-feed of (c) reaches the remaining string unfused up to F2's rating.
     (c) is bounded at 6.15 A by the vehicle entry, under 15 A, while that entry holds: the string's protection rests on (c)'s
     fault tree, not on F2 (INFERRED)
   the current page's 15 A equals the held sheet's: the review's figures do not move this row

7. THE COMBINED-FEED FUSE, LEAD AND CONNECTOR
   current: 1.25 x 14.70 A = 18.37 A, the standard step at or above it 20 A (INFERRED; a1solar ARRAY.md 4)
   voltage: at least 56.25 V DC (section 4)
   interrupting rating: at or above the prospective fault from the kit side at that voltage; NOT DERIVED (the source is the
     vehicle through a failed entry, a figure no record holds)
   as generated (NETLIST): F2 '10 A mini blade (Keystone 3568 holder): panel input'; J_SOLAR 'JST-VH socket, 10 A: bare panel in (lead from the D38999 spa'
   the lead, J_SOLAR, the wall's solar pair and F2's holder: at or above 20 A at 56.25 V (the conductor at or above the fuse that
     protects it)

